  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Chances for showers and thunderstorms will continue \nthrough the end of the week and into the weekend. Any thunderstorms \nthat do form my be capable of producing locally heavy downpours\nand gusty winds.\n\nWarm and humid conditions expected today (dewpoints in the mid/upper \n60s to around 70F). Highs again will climb firmly into the 80s, with \neven some locations approaching 90F. Heat index values will again \nrange from the upper 80s to low 90s in the warmest locations.  \n\nShowers and thunderstorm coverage will remain fairly sparse across \nfar western New York this afternoon. Even guidance suggests that PW \nvalues will fall off into the 1.2\" to 1.4\" range as drier air works \ninto the mid-levels. The further east you go it will be a bit of a \ndifferent story, largely from the Genesee Valley east across the \nFinger Lakes region and northeast into the North Country inland\naway from Lake Ontario. This is where deeper moisture (PW \nvalues +1.7) will be found, MLCAPE +2K, and somewhat better \nsupport aloft this afternoon and evening. Also...0-6km shear values \nof 25-35 knots may support a few storms to build enough to produce \nstrong gusty winds. However...the main threat will 'likely' be \nlocalized heavy rainfall. WPC continues to advertise all of the \nregion in a marginal risk for excessive rainfall given the overall \nhigh PW values. \n\nThe mid-level trough and cold front slowly inch east towards the \nregion Friday, with a better chance for widespread showers and \nthunderstorms in the morning and afternoon. Moisture will again tick \nup with PW values of +1.7\" across the region and MLCAPE values north \nof +2K inland from the lakes. Guidance suggest we might even see a \nconvectively augmented shortwave move through the region just before \nor around peak heating. We will need to keep an eye on this feature \nas it may aid in the severe wx potential Friday. \n\nFriday night and Saturday...we will see additional chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms as the cold front nears and then \neventually crosses the region. \n\nKey Message 2...Brief reprieve from the showers and \nthunderstorms Sunday, then unsettle weather returns Monday and \nTuesday. \n\nIt looks like we will see drier, cooler, and less humid conditions \nSunday behind the passage of the cold front. That said...it doesn't \nlast long as chances for showers and thunderstorms return \nMonday. We will also see a warming trend with humidity \nreturning which looks like it will be with us through atleast \nTuesday.",
